{title: Sent Eastward to the Land of the East}
{subtitle: Genesis 25:1–2; 25:5–6; 25:4; 1 Chronicles 1:32–33}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Abraham took another wife named Keturah
She bore him sons of a different line
[Bb]Midian was [F]born before the [C]end came
[Bb]One of the [C]six who were [Dm]his
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He gave everything he owned to Isaac
But [Bb]to the sons of his [C]concubines he gave [Dm]gifts
While [Bb]he was still a[F]live he sent them a[C]way
[Bb]Eastward to the [C]land of the [Dm]east
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sent [Bb]eastward to the [F]land of the [C]east
A[Bb]way from the in[F]heritance of I[C]saac
To the [Bb]sons of his con[F]cubines [C]he gave [Dm]gifts
[Bb]A separate path [C]in the eastern [Dm]light
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Ephah and Epher and Hanoch too
A[Bb]bida and [C]Eldaah are [Dm]named
The [Bb]sons of Midian [F]were the chil[C]dren
Of Ke[Bb]turah in the [C]ancient [Dm]days
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
All these were the sons of Keturah
Re[Bb]corded in the [C]books of [Dm]Chronicles
[Bb]Midian the [F]ancestor [C]of the clans
[Bb]Lived in the [C]areas south and [Dm]east
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sent [Bb]eastward to the [F]land of the [C]east
A[Bb]way from the in[F]heritance of I[C]saac
To the [Bb]sons of his con[F]cubines [C]he gave [Dm]gifts
[Bb]A separate [C]path in the eastern [Dm]light
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Eastward to the [F]land of the [C]east
Sent a[Bb]way while [C]he was still a[Dm]live
{end_of_verse}
